     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Common initial regimens for most ART-naive adults are INSTI-based (eg, bictegravir/TAF/emtricitabine; dolutegravir + TAF or TDF + emtricitabine or lamivudine; dolutegravir/lamivudine). Not dolutegravir/lamivudine if HIV RNA >500,000 copies/mL, HBV coinfection, or before genotype and HBV results are back."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Dolutegravir:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 50 mg PO once daily (ART-naive or INSTI-naive adults)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " prior hypersensitivity to dolutegravir; dofetilide (↑ dofetilide levels, serious/life-threatening events)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Take dolutegravir 2 h before or 6 h after cation antacids/laxatives, sucralfate, iron or calcium supplements, buffered meds (with food, calcium or iron can be taken together). Bictegravir is CI with rifampin or rifabutin (↓ levels, ART failure)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Hypersensitivity (rash, constitutional sx, sometimes organ dysfunction incl. liver injury; <1%): stop at once. Hepatotoxicity, higher risk with HBV or HCV; monitor. INSTIs are the class most linked to weight gain."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
